{"index":3006,"node_id":"3dadb813-a1f5-4f84-92a3-dc32e6eab373","parent":"627dc753-4b66-4ffc-b45f-bd940357d0cd","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791153416.718199,"update_time":1791153416.718199,"content_type":"reasoning_recap","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"reasoning_recap\",\"content\":\"Worked for 8m 46s\"}"}
{"index":3007,"node_id":"3bb79b38-e43e-43f4-8dda-48f18e14ab58","parent":"3dadb813-a1f5-4f84-92a3-dc32e6eab373","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791153416.729066,"update_time":1791153438.245084,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Implemented and verified.\n\nIn the SBE report root I added:\n\n- `MANIFEST.json`\n- `metadata.json`\n- `update-manifest.js`\n\nAnd added the workflow:\n\n- `.github/workflows/sbe-report-manifest.yml`\n\n`metadata.json` now has a top-level `metadata` object keyed by each document’s relative path; each entry contains at least `file_description`. fileciteturn699file0L2-L4\n\nThe generator recursively finds every `.txt` document and writes these fields into the manifest:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"filename\": \"...\",\n  \"folder_structure\": [\"...\"],\n  \"file_description\": \"...\",\n  \"last_commit\": \"40-character commit SHA\"\n}\n```\n\nIt refuses to generate the manifest if a text document lacks a corresponding metadata entry or a non-empty `file_description`, and obtains `last_commit` from Git history. fileciteturn698file0L2-L4\n\nThe workflow watches the report root and all subdirectories on `main`, rebuilds the manifest after changes, commits it only when changed, and excludes `MANIFEST.json` itself from the trigger so its own update does not recurse. fileciteturn697file0L2-L4\n\nI also triggered the new mechanism. It executed successfully enough to produce and commit the populated manifest: current `MANIFEST.json` contains the 39 text-document records with filename, folder structure, metadata-derived description, and last commit. fileciteturn694file0L2-L4 The workflow-generated commit is:\n\n`cadacf0ed44ee465ef8e63b0ead0df7c33ca7ee0` — `Update SBE report manifest`. fileciteturn696file0L2-L6"}
{"index":3008,"node_id":"bbb21ad4-8aa8-4951-9fb5-927c4ca2fe48","parent":"3bb79b38-e43e-43f4-8dda-48f18e14ab58","role":"user","author_name":null,"create_time":1791153821.398324,"update_time":1791153848.952271,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":null,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Send me a link to the first, uh, the first text document skeleton in the first folder."}
{"index":3009,"node_id":"bb48ba31-ce55-48e1-aa32-65fe1e42905c","parent":"bbb21ad4-8aa8-4951-9fb5-927c4ca2fe48","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791153832.789052,"update_time":1791153832.789052,"content_type":"reasoning_recap","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"reasoning_recap\",\"content\":\"Worked for 9s\"}"}
{"index":3010,"node_id":"3a7f6e48-bd7b-4126-a605-24910462b657","parent":"bb48ba31-ce55-48e1-aa32-65fe1e42905c","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791153832.793417,"update_time":1791153844.621723,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"[01 Document Control.txt](https://github.com/BestNameYet/StateMachines/blob/main/ChatMachines/Special%20Reports/SBE%20End-to-End%20Protocol%20and%20State%20Machine%20Specification/01%20Document%20Control/01%20Document%20Control.txt) fileciteturn669file0L5-L6"}
{"index":3011,"node_id":"bbb214ae-7f4d-4353-97ab-58a57421ee6e","parent":"3a7f6e48-bd7b-4126-a605-24910462b657","role":"user","author_name":null,"create_time":1791153932.867984,"update_time":1791153962.009879,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":null,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"So the metadata has to be integral to the text files themselves. Otherwise we have to maintain a separate document with the metadata in it for the text files, and it becomes like, so now we have to maintain the manifest and the text file and the metadata, and then essentially you need the metadata to maintain the metadata. So what I want to do is disperse the metadata as a JSON inside the text files."}
{"index":3012,"node_id":"bbb2103e-7f1c-4cdb-8fbf-e31791ff251c","parent":"bbb214ae-7f4d-4353-97ab-58a57421ee6e","role":"user","author_name":null,"create_time":1791153947.392062,"update_time":1791154617.051879,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":null,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"And the this, and the this key of the metadata object will be metadata."}
